    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: None that materially matter here (e.g., minor formatting differences would be fine if the underlying values were clearly correct and sourced).\n\nCritical issues: (1) Release Date is reported as \u201cJun 1, 1998\u201d but there is no screenshot evidence showing the \u201cRelease Date\u201d label/value on the page at all. Given the task\u2019s explicit constraint to use the Gutenberg label (not a known publication date), this is effectively unsupported and could be fabricated. (2) Last Update is reported as \u201cSep 1, 2026,\u201d also with no visible evidence of a \u201cLast Update\u201d label/value; this is again unsupported and very likely incorrect. (3) The agent reports \u201cPlain Text (accessible) \u2014 Available\u201d and \u201cDownload HTML (zip) \u2014 Available,\u201d but the provided screenshots only visibly show the EPUB3 option; the other two exact labels are not visible anywhere in the evidence. While it\u2019s possible they exist further down the page, the agent did not capture/confirm them in the provided evidence, making these availability claims unsupported.\n\nWhat is supported: The agent did access a Project Gutenberg Pride and Prejudice page, and the \u201cAbout this eBook\u201d table in Screenshot 2 supports Author = \u201cAusten, Jane, 1775-1817\u201d and Language = \u201cEnglish.\u201d Screenshot 1 supports that the \u201cEPUB3\u201d format label is available.\n\nOutcome assessment: The task\u2019s primary deliverable is a complete and accurate record of all four metadata fields plus the availability of all three specified formats, using the Gutenberg labels exactly. Because two of the four required metadata fields (Release Date and Last Update) are provided without evidence and two of the three format availability checks are also provided without evidence, the agent did not reliably complete the task from the user\u2019s perspective. The user would not accept potentially invented dates/format availability for a fact-checking task with explicit label/accuracy constraints.",
